# Development and review material (reconnaissance, plans, per-stage reports,
# validation evidence).  Kept on disk for review, deliberately not versioned.
# The three delivery documents are the exception: they are the published
# contract of the landscape suite (PLAN, M7 validation) and of the CLI
# redesign, and are versioned.
#
# --- documentation site corpus: versioned (owner ruling D1) -----------------
# The site corpus at docs/docs-site/ is versioned; the rest of docs/ stays
# untracked.  git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded,
# so the excluded component (docs/docs-site) is re-included first; its contents
# then need no rule because docs/* does not cross "/".  Do NOT add
# "!docs/docs-site/**": as the last matching pattern it would override every
# artifact rule above and stage suite artefacts (landscape_*.json, xtbopt.xyz,
# hessian, vibspectrum, xtbscan.log, site/, __pycache__/, ...) into the repo.
docs/*
!docs/xtb-landscape-PLAN.md
!docs/xtb-landscape-M7-validation.md
!docs/xtb-cli-redesign-delivery.md
!docs/docs-site/
# `mkdocs build` output and the generated pages never enter git; their single
# source of truth is src/xhelp.f90, man/*.adoc and the Fortran sources.
# The API directory is special: generated FORD output is ignored, but the
# hand-written entry point `api/index.md` is tracked, so the rule ignores the
# directory *contents* (`api/*`) and re-includes the stub.  The directory form
# `docs/docs-site/docs/api/` (trailing slash) must NOT be used: git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so the `!` line could never re-include
# the stub.
docs/docs-site/site/
docs/docs-site/docs/cli/
docs/docs-site/docs/man/
docs/docs-site/docs/api/*
!docs/docs-site/docs/api/index.md
